<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 13 August, from 523 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/papacy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/papacy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">523 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,503 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John I becomes pope after the death of Hormisdas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John I, a native of Siena, succeeded Pope Hormisdas as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He helped standardise the Western reckoning of Easter, and died in 526 after imprisonment by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoth</a> king Theoderic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">582 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,444 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The dying Tiberius II crowns Maurice as Byzantine emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Maurice, a successful general whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> II had chosen as his heir and son-in-law, was crowned emperor by the dying Tiberius. He reigned until 602, the last emperor of the Justinian dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/900">900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zwentibold of Lotharingia is killed in battle on the Meuse</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwentibold">Zwentibold</a>, king of Lotharingia since 895, was killed in battle on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> near present-day Susteren by nobles who had risen against him under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginar-duke-of-lorraine">Reginar Longneck</a>. Lotharingia then passed to his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-child">Louis the Child</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwentibold">Zwentibold</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginar-duke-of-lorraine">Reginar Longneck</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1099">1099 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">927 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paschal II is elected pope in succession to Urban II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Raniero Raineri di <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleda">Bleda</a>, a monk of Cluny, was elected pope as Paschal II after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a> the previous month. His reign of almost twenty years was exceptionally long for a medieval pope.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tenochtitlan falls to Cortés and his allies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of nearly three months, Spanish forces and their Tlaxcalan allies captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a> and the Aztec capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, rose on its ruins.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1704">1704 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">322 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marlborough and Prince Eugene win the Battle of Blenheim</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-churchill-1st-duke-of-marlborough">Duke of Marlborough</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a> destroyed a Franco-Bavarian army at Blenheim. The victory saved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and knocked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Netherlands cedes the Cape Colony to Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Convention of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, the Dutch formally ceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> had occupied since 1806. British rule shaped southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> for the following century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1898">1898 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US forces take Manila from Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> after a largely staged battle with the Spanish garrison, unaware that a peace protocol had been signed the day before. The US went on to annex the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">East Germany seals the border in Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Overnight, East German forces closed the crossings and began building barriers that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a>. For 28 years it divided the city, and at least 140 people died trying to cross.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 August <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xi-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-xi-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso XI of Castile</span><span class="tp">1311–1350</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-bruhl"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/heinrich-von-bruhl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Heinrich von Brühl</span><span class="tp">1700–1763</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/makarios-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/makarios-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Makarios III</span><span class="tp">1913–1977</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fidel-castro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fidel Castro</span><span class="tp">1926–2016</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 August <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/radegund"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Radegund</span><span class="tp">c. 520–587</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-wen-of-sui.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Wen of Sui</span><span class="tp">541–604</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/zwentibold"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zwentibold.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Zwentibold</span><span class="tp">c. 870–900</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/filippo-maria-visconti"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/filippo-maria-visconti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Filippo Maria Visconti</span><span class="tp">1392–1447</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ahilyabai-holkar"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Ahilyabai Holkar</span><span class="tp">1725–1795</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ignaz-semmelweis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ignaz-semmelweis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ignaz Semmelweis</span><span class="tp">1818–1865</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-lange"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-lange.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David Lange</span><span class="tp">1942–2005</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
